Vendor Contract Renewal Management

Purpose

To establish a consistent process for identifying upcoming vendor contract renewals and avoiding missed notice deadlines.

Recommended tracking fields

Field	Description
Vendor name	Contracting supplier
Contract owner	Internal accountable person
Contract reference	Unique contract identifier
Effective date	Contract commencement
Expiry date	Contract end date
Renewal type	Automatic or manual
Notice period	Required advance notice
Notice deadline	Latest date for termination notice
Annual contract value	Approved financial commitment
Renewal decision	Renew, renegotiate or terminate
Approval status	Pending or approved

Suggested review schedule

* 120 days before expiry: Initial performance and spend review.
* 90 days before expiry: Begin commercial and business assessment.
* 60 days before expiry: Complete required negotiations and approvals.
* 30 days before expiry: Confirm decision and execute required actions.

Actual deadlines must always follow the relevant contract terms.

Renewal decision considerations

* Vendor performance.
* Pricing and market competitiveness.
* Business need.
* Security and privacy posture.
* Financial commitments.
* Alternative suppliers.
* Contractual notice requirements.

Control principle: Every active contract should have an assigned owner and a clearly documented renewal or termination decision.